TEXT -256 -288 Left 3 ;#412 Common-emitter amplifier - gain with the output unloaded
TEXT -256 -232 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yhuf2_Zu8T8
TEXT -256 -184 Left 2 ;A 2N2222 common-emitter stage with an unbypassed 1k emitter. CH1 probes the base, CH2 the collector, with nothing loading the output.
TEXT 944 -128 Left 2 !.tran 0 20m 16m 1u
TEXT 944 -80 Left 2 !.meas tran CH1_PP PP V(base) FROM 16m TO 20m
TEXT 944 -32 Left 2 !.meas tran CH2_PP PP V(collector) FROM 16m TO 20m
TEXT 944 16 Left 2 !.meas tran GAIN PARAM CH2_PP/CH1_PP
TEXT 944 64 Left 2 !.meas tran VB_DC AVG V(base)
TEXT 944 112 Left 2 !.meas tran VC_DC AVG V(collector)
TEXT 944 192 Left 2 ;GAIN repeats Alan's math trace: CH2 amplitude divided by CH1 amplitude.
TEXT 944 240 Left 2 ;VB_DC and VC_DC are the DC levels his AC-coupled channels remove.
TEXT -256 432 Left 2 ;Alan's resistor substitution box is set to 0 here, so only the generator's own 50 ohm output impedance is in the path.
TEXT -256 480 Left 2 ;RLOAD 1Meg stands in for the open output terminal, which LTspice needs for a DC path.
